    "pdp_faq": {
      "type": "glowve-pdp-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will this leave a white cast on my skin tone?",
            "answer": "<p>No. This formula uses only chemical UV filters — no zinc oxide or titanium dioxide, which are the minerals that cause white cast. Chemical filters are colourless and designed for Fitzpatrick III–VI skin tones. If you've had white cast issues with other SPFs, it's because they used mineral filters. This one won't.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I really need SPF even on cloudy days in Pakistan?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — especially UVA. Clouds block roughly 20% of UV. UVA (the kind that causes PIH, tanning, and aging) penetrates cloud cover and glass. In Pakistan, even on overcast winter days in Islamabad, UVA levels are significant. If you skip SPF on cloudy days, you're cancelling 2–3 days of serum progress with every missed application.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use this as a primer under makeup?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — it works excellently as a primer base. Apply, wait 2 minutes to set, then apply makeup. The matte finish actually helps foundation adhere better. No pilling reported with any foundation format.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
